      "items": [
        {
          "published_at": "2026-10-14T21:52:18.460Z",
          "url": "https://x.com/trq212/status/2110488896039690255",
          "topic": "The detail-oriented skill of coding-agent work",
          "text": "@fnthawar and I talked about how the skill of coding agents is \"being in the details\"\n\nlike running a company, you can't know everything but caring obsessively about the right details is what makes something great\n\nit could be code, architecture, design, UX- whatevers needed",
          "quote_tweet": {
            "url": "https://x.com/trq212/status/2110035114432532654",
            "published_at": "2026-10-13T15:49:08.494Z",
            "author": {
              "name": "Thariq",
              "handle": "trq212"
            },
            "text": "excited to be back home",
            "media": [
              {
                "type": "photo",
                "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUhZgBeXMAAkXxm?format=webp&name=large",
                "width": 450,
                "height": 600
              }
            ]
          },
          "author_replies": [
            {
              "url": "https://x.com/trq212/status/2110488897453257169",
              "published_at": "2026-10-14T21:52:18.797Z",
              "author": {
                "name": "Thariq",
                "handle": "trq212"
              },
              "text": "I used to tell people it's good to \"be technical\" but I think this is not accurate enough. \n\nIf you're technical you need to be in the details more with the right parts of the code.\n\nIf you're non-technical, being in the details means knowing how things work at the right level.",
              "media": []
            }
          ],
